      "body": "### Version\n\nWelcome to Node.js v26.2.0.\n\n### Platform\n\n```text\nMicrosoft Windows NT 10.0.26200.0 x64\n```\n\n### Subsystem\n\n_No response_\n\n### What steps will reproduce the bug?\n\n\nWelcome to Node.js v26.2.0.\nType \".help\" for more information.\n>\n> function     exec_sql_once(dbpath, sql) {\n|         const { DatabaseSync } = require('node:sqlite');\n|         const db = new DatabaseSync(dbpath, { readOnly: true });\n|         return db.prepare(sql).all();\n|     }\nundefined\n> s='D:/FFMPEG-RTSP-CLIENT/rtsp-win-server/rtsp_server/PUBLISH/___webvw___/userDataFolder/EBWebView/Default/History'\n'D:/FFMPEG-RTSP-CLIENT/rtsp-win-server/rtsp_server/PUBLISH/___webvw___/userDataFolder/EBWebView/Default/History'\n> exec_sql_once(s,\"SELECT * FROM urls;\")\nUncaught:\nRangeError: Value is too large to be represented as a JavaScript number: 13435075631098976\n    at exec_sql_once (REPL6:4:32) {\n  code: 'ERR_OUT_OF_RANGE'\n}\n>\n>\n\n### How often does it reproduce? Is there a required condition?\n\nalways\n\n### What is the expected behavior? Why is that the expected behavior?\n\nto bigint OR string instead of  'ERR_OUT_OF_RANGE'\n\n### What do you see instead?\n\nUncaught:\nRangeError: Value is too large to be represented as a JavaScript number: 13435075631098976\n    at exec_sql_once (REPL6:4:32) {\n  code: 'ERR_OUT_OF_RANGE'\n}\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_",
